    {
      "key": "lesson-2",
      "name": "generating a lesson",
      "absolute_position": 2,
      "lockable": false,
      "has_lesson_plan": true,
      "relative_position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "generate_outline": "Lesson 4: Making Decisions with if\nQuestion of the Day: How do computers choose between different paths of action?\nObjectives:\nIdentify and use Comparison Operators (==, !=, >, <).\nConstruct a basic if and else statement in Python.\nTrace the flow of a program when a condition is met versus when it is not.\nLesson Outline:\nWarm-up: Real-life \"If-Then\" logic (e.g., If it is raining, then I wear a jacket).\nComparison Syntax: Introducing the \"Double Equals\" (==) for comparison vs the \"Single Equals\" (=) for assignment.\nThe Indentation Rule: Explaining how Python uses whitespace to define code blocks.\nActivity: Building a \"Smart Home\" controller that reacts to environmental data.\nWrap-up: Checking for understanding via a Free Response exit ticket."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "lesson.key": "lesson-2",
        "lesson_group.key": "",
        "script.name": "jamila-sandbox"
      }
    }
  ],
